 "decisions": [
  "Route vents stand on the trail as timing gates (tiny, non-colliding); flank vents are at least 18 studs from it so their discs never touch the corridor.",
  "Neighbouring route vents run half a cycle apart (phase 0 or 5.75 s) so they never erupt together, and the 2.5 s glow is longer than the 1.25 s it takes to cross a whole disc at 16 studs/s.",
  "Cool stones are read as refuge markers: four per route vent and per shrine, outside the corridor and every disc. The bible only calls them walkable slabs; this meaning is a draft choice.",
  "Crust plates are dressing in four fields at least 30 studs from the trail; they carry no hazard meaning.",
  "Obsidian shards: 12 along the trail, 6 beside flank vents with the gather point just outside the disc (reward beside danger, never inside it).",
  "Columns and trees keep sight lanes clear: every route vent is visible from 40 studs upstream.",
  "Shrines straddle the trail near both gates with the measured gap (about 0 off centre) centred on the trail; the pivot sits on the centreline.",
  "Footprints are bounding circles of the measured geometry, including tree branches (8.7)."
 ],
